00:01:08.190 --> 00:01:12.500
So the story is as follows, a 27 year old
Alabama woman was shot in the stomach while

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:17.920
pregnant and she was shot by another woman
and being shot in the stomach resulted in

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:18.920
a miscarriage.

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:24.900
Um, she is now being charged with manslaughter
for that miscarriage, which of course is connected

00:01:24.900 --> 00:01:28.340
to her being the victim of a shooting.

00:01:28.340 --> 00:01:31.480
So there's a whole bunch of details here that
can be discussed.

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:37.170
One is that the fight that led to the shooting
was between the pregnant woman Marshae Jones

00:01:37.170 --> 00:01:41.450
and another woman who were fighting over the
fetus's father.

00:01:41.450 --> 00:01:48.480
Um, the shooter, Ebony Jamison, was charged
with manslaughter initially and not indicted

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:49.640
by a grand jury.

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:51.380
So that charge was dismissed.

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:54.710
Now Jones has been indicted on a manslaughter
charge.

00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:59.909
The argument being made by police in pleasant
grove, Alabama is that the mother instigated

00:01:59.909 --> 00:02:04.820
the argument with the other woman that the
victim here is the unborn fetus.

00:02:04.820 --> 00:02:09.920
And were it not for the instigation of the
mother that none of this would have happened.

00:02:09.920 --> 00:02:12.340
Therefore, the mother should be charged with
manslaughter.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:18.060
Now you might laugh this off and say, Alabama,
this wouldn't happen anywhere else.

00:02:18.060 --> 00:02:19.060
That's not true.

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:26.260
There are 38 states that classify fetuses
as victims in homicide or assault.

00:02:26.260 --> 00:02:28.630
And the truth is that sometimes that does
make sense.

00:02:28.630 --> 00:02:29.630
Okay.

00:02:29.630 --> 00:02:35.890
If a burglary gone wrong, leads to a burglar
shooting a pregnant woman and both the woman

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:37.450
and the fetus die.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:44.030
The fact that there was the potential for
life there and that to actual or potential

00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:48.150
lives were cut short should be considered
by the law.

00:02:48.150 --> 00:02:54.240
The problem is that in places like Alabama,
it's being applied in really ridiculous ways

00:02:54.240 --> 00:03:00.151
that truly stretched credulity and require,
I, I mean I, I'd call it imagination and in

00:03:00.151 --> 00:03:03.190
a sense are criminalizing of pregnancy.

00:03:03.190 --> 00:03:09.610
And the reason that lots of, uh, anti choice
activists love this indictment is they understand,

00:03:09.610 --> 00:03:15.590
they understand the long game and they see
